export interface Scenario {
  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };
  steps: Step[];
}

export type Item = {
  type: string;
  material?: string;
  enchantment?: number;
  cursed?: boolean;
};

export type Step =
  | { op: "quote"; items: Item[] }
  | {
      op: "claim";
      policy: number;
      incident: { cause: string; damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[] };
    };

parts.text:
Now, this test requires restructuring the pricing model to support item-specific surcharges. This is a substantial green change. Let me rewrite the pricing logic.

Key requirements from this test:
- Amulet base premium 60 (`MAIN_ITEMS.amulet = 60`)
- Cursed surcharge = 50% of the cursed item's base premium, applied per affected item
- Policy base premium (block-discounted sum) used for policy-wide first-insurance

I also need to think about how `quotePremium` will handle: base + cursed surcharges (item-specific) then first-insurance on base then fee. And `runScenario` needs a first-contract determination. But the first-insurance is applied on the policy base for now (all our scenarios so far are first contract). Let me keep `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE` applied on base for now (all current tests are first contracts), and worry about loyalty/followup later.

Let me restructure:

```ts
const MAIN_ITEMS: Record<string, number> = { sword: 100, amulet: 60 };
...
const CURSE_RATE = 0.5;

function itemBasePremium(item: Item): number {
  return isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_PREMIUM : MAIN_ITEMS[item.type];
}

function computeItemSurcharges(items: Item[]): number {
  let total = 0;
  for (const item of items) {
    if (item.cursed) {
      total += CURSE_RATE * itemBasePremium(item);
    }
  }
  return total;
}
```

And quotePremium:
```ts
function quotePremium(items: Item[]) {
  const base = computeBasePremium(items);
  const surcharges = computeItemSurcharges(items);
  const firstInsurance = FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE * base;
  return Math.ceil(base + surcharges + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);
}
```

This keeps the existing tests passing (no cursed items before, so surcharges=0). Let me apply.

